{"abstract":"Let $G$ be a complete edge-weighted graph on $n$ vertices. To each subset of vertices of $G$ assign the cost of the minimum spanning tree of the subset as its weight. Suppose that $n$ is a multiple of some fixed positive integer $k$. The $k$-matching problem is the problem of finding a partition of the vertices of $G$ into $k$-sets, that minimizes the sum of the weights of the $k$-sets. The case $k=3$ has been shown to be NP-hard [Johnsson et al.,1998]. In the Euclidean version, the vertices of $G$ are points in the plane and the weight of an edge is the Euclidean distance between its endpoints. We call this problem the Euclidean $k$-matching problem. We show that, for every fixed $k \\ge 3$, the Euclidean $k$-matching is NP-hard. This resolves an open problem in the literature and provides the first theoretical justification for the use of known heuristic methods in the case $k=3$. We also show that the problem remains NP-hard if the trees are required to be paths.","affiliations":[],"arxiv_id":"2502.15660","authors":["José-Miguel Díaz-Báñez","Ruy Fabila-Monroy","José-Manuel Higes-López","Nestaly Marín","Miguel-Angel Pérez-Cutiño","Pablo Pérez-Lantero"],"availability":{"basis":"arxiv_public_full_text","checked_at":"2026-08-21T05:34:26+00:00","full_text_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2502.15660.pdf","license":"arxiv-distribution","page_count":18,"pdf_bytes":893729,"status":"available"},"citation_count":null,"content_digest":"4b13ef3730f7cc9367bd308d8be746ef4510b0ef6e94e766f5be31b069459e08","created_at":"2026-08-21T05:34:26+00:00","doi":"","identifier_observations":[],"institutions":[],"landing_url":"","legacy_ids":[],"migration_provenance":{"source_content_digest":"33feac6fb6656b4005c3d7782cff4264fc873dbb9841339b5a1ad2fdb72ef4f1","source_schema_version":"global-work-v1"},"openalex_id":"","pmcid":"","pmid":"","publication_date":"","revision":1,"schema_version":"global-work-v2","semantic_scholar_id":"","source_urls":[],"status":"active","title":"The Euclidean $k$-Matching Problem is NP-hard","updated_at":"2026-08-21T05:34:26+00:00","venue":"arXiv","work_id":"W-49E2D55EC425","year":2025}
